      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0",
      "artist": "Georgia National Guard from United States",
      "description": "FORT JACKSON, Savannah, Ga. April 12, 2015 – Georgia Army National Guard Lt Col. David S. Allen entrusts Command Sgt. Maj. Scott Payton with the colors of the 1st Battalion, 118th Field Artillery Regiment following his assumption of command from Lt. Col. Kevin Hamm. \nWitnessing the change of command was Col. Reginald Neal, commander of the 48th Infantry Brigade Combat Team and former commander of the 118th FA.\nThe 118th FA traces its lineage to 1751 and its colors bear campaign streamers from the American Revolution, the War of 1812, the American Civil War, The Spanish American War, World War I, and World War II. Recently, the battalion has added campaign streamers from Iraq and Afghanistan to its storied record of battle honors.  \n\nGeorgia Army National Guard photo by 2nd Lt. Samantha Hutchinson, 1-118th Field Artillery / released",
