      "artist": "Georgia National Guard from United States",
      "description": "FORT JACKSON, Savannah, Ga. April 12, 2015 – Smoke from modern 105 mm artillery pieces and Civil War-era 32-lb cannons mingled in the air at old Fort Jackson following the change of command ceremony for the Georgia Army National Guard’s historic 1st Battalion, 118th Field Artillery Regiment. Lieutenant Colonel David Allen assumed command from Lt. Col. Kevin Hamm in a ceremony that highlighted the long history of the 118th FA, who as the Chatham Artillery, was stationed at Fort Jackson during the War of 1812.\n\nGeorgia Army National Guard photo by 2nd Lt. Samantha Hutchinson, 1-118th Field Artillery / released",
